        },
        {
          "text": " “Judge not, that you be not judged. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 7:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For with the judgment you pronounce you will be judged, and the measure you give will be the measure you get. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 7:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.6.41+LUK.6.42"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lk 6.41-42",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Why do you see the speck that is in your brother's eye, but do not notice the log that is in your own eye? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 7:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Or how can you say to your brother, ‘Let me take the speck out of your eye,’ when there is the log in your own eye? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 7:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You hypocrite, first take the log out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to take the speck out of your brother's eye.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
