        },
        {
          "text": " “Enter by the narrow gate; for the gate is wide and the way is easy,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.13",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Other ancient authorities read",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "for the way is wide and easy",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " that leads to destruction, and those who enter by it are many. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 7:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the gate is narrow and the way is hard, that leads to life, and those who find it are few.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.7.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.7.14"
            ]
          }
        }
